    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="1016" n="922" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg922"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1896</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 992.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information the copy of a dispatch from Acting Consular Agent A. H. Poche at
                    Aleppo, dated the 11th instant, which refers to the condition of the naturalized
                    Americans now in prison at Aleppo. The men in prison were arrested in armed
                    resistance to the Government, and surrendered on the promise that they would be
                    sent from the country.</p>
                <p>The situation of the prisoners remains unchanged, and in the present condition of
                    unrest and suspicion but little can be hoped for beyond saving their lives.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d881-a1.xml" xpointer="d881-a1"/>
